# Book II "The Far Shore", solo, BOTH difficulties, from a fresh save, through the 2.0 title path (docs/expansion/PLAN.md
# 6.2, DESIGN.md A.1 / A.2): title -> Play -> Solo -> book select (Book II) -> Beginner -> the Far Shore map -> every
# Beginner stop of Book II in order, each stage played by its club route (`<id>.inputs`, LEVEL_DESIGN.md 15.9), the
# linked stages without a tally, the bosses Tusker, Old Mangrove and Inkjaw, every tally, the expert wall after Squid
# Grotto; then the title again -> Book II -> Expert -> every stop with its Expert routes (`<id>.expert.inputs`, an
# Expert-only stage's `<id>.inputs`) through worlds 8 and 9, the Twin Idols, the Storm Roc, the Rival Chieftains, the
# Great Roast's trophy into the Long Raft Home, its tally and The End. The run carries what a player's run carries
# (score, lives, letters, hand and belt); no weapon is ever handed over. Checks: no life lost, the club in hand at
# every stage start (the fresh-club rule), the map stop recorded in the run's save space after each tally, Book II and
# solo mode, the wall without completing the book, The End with it. Named screenshots of every map stop, stage start
# and tally, one every 480 ticks of play.
# The headless twin is tests/test_book2_routes.gd test_the_book2_{beginner,expert}_campaign_in_one_run (the same
# routes, the same run). Beginner visits both Feast Lands: 5-1 by its painting route, which leaves with the spear
# (w5_l1.painting.inputs), so the fresh-club rule puts the spear on the belt for 5-2, whose warp needs two spear steps
# (w5_l2.warp.inputs, then bonus_d.inputs; the warp passes the Tusker stage 5-2b, which the Expert part fights), and
# 7-1's warp into Feast Land E (w7_l1.warp.inputs, bonus_e.inputs).
# Every stop begins with `need` - its files and routes. Until phase 3 was content complete this was a skeleton flow
# (a stop whose content had not landed ended its section, PENDING); at G3 (Book II complete) the skeleton line went,
# so a missing `need` fails the run.
# Two parts (`section`): each starts at the title.
#   GD_TIMEOUT=3600 bash .tools/gd.sh play --flow=tools/autoplay/campaign_b2.flow --fast --fresh-user --out=campaign_b2
# Headless (no screenshots; tools/g3.sh runs it so):
#   GD_TIMEOUT=3600 bash .tools/gd.sh script res://scripts/core/dev/headless_flow.gd -- \
#       --flow=tools/autoplay/campaign_b2.flow --fast --fresh-user --user-dir=res://build/flow_user_campaign_b2

########################################################################################################################
# Solo, Book II, Beginner
########################################################################################################################
section book2_beginner
# Every part counts its own events: a stage that fails in one part (a wipe, a death) must not fail the
# `== 0` checks of the parts after it.
reset_events

# --- Title, Play > Solo > Book II > Beginner --------------------------------------------------------------------------
wait_until flow.current_screen == title 900
wait_until flow.busy == false 600
wait 40
shot title_book2_beginner
expect save.has_progress() == false
# Play, then Solo (Flow.open_play; Solo has the focus, Co-op is one down).
press ui_accept
wait 10
press ui_accept
wait_until flow.current_screen == book_select 300
wait_until flow.busy == false 600
# The book select has Book I focused (Flow.play_book); Right = Book II.
press ui_right
wait 10
shot book_select_book2_beginner
press ui_accept
wait_until flow.current_screen == mode_select 300
wait_until flow.busy == false 600
expect flow.play_book == 2
# Left = Beginner, Right = Expert, whichever card the last run left focused.
press ui_left
wait 10
shot mode_select_book2_beginner
press ui_accept
wait_until flow.current_screen == world_map 600
wait_until flow.busy == false 600
expect game.book == 2
expect game.mode == 0
expect game.party == 1
expect game.difficulty == 0
expect game.lives == 2
expect game.score == 0
expect game.weapon == 0

# --- w5_l1, by its painting route (it ends with the spear in hand) -----------------------------------------------------
# As the headless twin (tests/test_book2_routes.gd CAMPAIGN_SIDES): the painting on the way, the spear picked up, a
# swap for the club line, the spear back in hand before the exit (w5_l1.painting.inputs, weapon_end:spear).
need w5_l1 tools/autoplay/routes/w5_l1.painting.inputs
wait_until flow.current_screen == world_map 900
wait_until flow.busy == false 600
expect flow.args.level_id == w5_l1
wait_until scene.countdown >= 0 600
shot map_w5_l1_book2_beginner
press ui_accept
wait_until flow.current_screen == level 900
wait_until flow.busy == false 600
wait_until level.level_id == w5_l1 600
expect hero.dead == false
# Fresh club (DESIGN.md C.1 rule 4): every Book II and co-op stage starts with the club in hand.
expect game.weapon == 0
wait 2
shot w5_l1_start
every 480 w5_l1
play_file tools/autoplay/routes/w5_l1.painting.inputs
every 0
expect events.player_died == 0
# The spear leaves 5-1 in hand: the next stage starts with the club and the spear on the belt.
expect game.weapon == 4
wait_until flow.current_screen == tally 900
wait_until flow.busy == false 600
wait 30
shot tally_w5_l1_book2_beginner
press ui_accept
wait 20
press ui_accept
# On to the map (checked by the next stop, after its `need`).

# --- w5_l2, by its warp into Feast Land D -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# As the headless twin (CAMPAIGN_SIDES): the spear carried over from 5-1 rides on the belt (the fresh-club rule); two
# spear steps reach the warp on the mesa pillar (w5_l2.warp.inputs); Feast Land D follows without a tally and its
# tally ends 5-2 - the warp passes the linked Tusker stage 5-2b (the Expert part plays 5-2 and 5-2b by their routes).
need w5_l2 bonus_d tools/autoplay/routes/w5_l2.warp.inputs tools/autoplay/routes/bonus_d.inputs
wait_until flow.current_screen == world_map 900
wait_until flow.busy == false 600
expect flow.args.level_id == w5_l2
expect save.get_level_result_in(single/book2/beginner,w5_l1).clears == 1
expect save.is_level_unlocked_in(single/book2/beginner,w5_l2) == true
wait_until scene.countdown >= 0 600
shot map_w5_l2_book2_beginner
press ui_accept
wait_until flow.current_screen == level 900
wait_until flow.busy == false 600
wait_until level.level_id == w5_l2 600
expect hero.dead == false
# Fresh club (DESIGN.md C.1 rule 4): the club in hand, what the hero carried - the spear of 5-1 - on the belt.
expect game.weapon == 0
expect game.get_run(0).belt == 4
wait 2
shot w5_l2_start
every 480 w5_l2
play_file tools/autoplay/routes/w5_l2.warp.inputs
every 0
expect events.player_died == 0
wait_until flow.current_screen == level 900
wait_until flow.busy == false 600
wait_until level.level_id == bonus_d 600
expect hero.dead == false
expect game.warp_return_level == w5_l2
wait 2
shot bonus_d_start
every 480 bonus_d
play_file tools/autoplay/routes/bonus_d.inputs
every 0
expect events.player_died == 0
wait_until flow.current_screen == tally 900
wait_until flow.busy == false 600
wait 30
shot tally_bonus_d_book2_beginner
press ui_accept
wait 20
press ui_accept
# On to the map (checked by the next stop, after its `need`).

